(out/'README.md').write_text('''# Cut Through — 8 November 2026

[Watch the film](Cut%20Through.mp4) · [Director and review controls](Director%20and%20native%20review%20refinement.mp4) · [Edit keys and sound](Edit%20motion%20keys%20and%20sound%20in%20Studio.mp4) · [Live Studio timeline](Complete%20live%20Studio%20playback.mp4) · [Finished film in Studio](Complete%20finished%20playback%20in%20Studio.mp4).

The moving city splits into five tall fragments over cobalt. The fan holds, leaves upward and hands off to five arriving ocean fragments. Those strips reconstruct as one clean ocean shot. No circular windows, translucent footage mixing or words in the film. The native result is eight seconds,192 frames,24fps,1280×720,H.264/AAC.

Director chose a bounded fragment-transition draft. Native review controls then lengthened its pacing to hold/fan/switch/resolve at1/3/5/7 seconds. The source-region repeater calculates exact source partitions and geometry; every evaluated effect remains in the ordinary Studio project. Twelve layers, ten Parent connections and265 keys remain editable. The score and two whooshes were manually selected. This is Director-assisted creation with explicit review refinement, not unrestricted autonomous AE/Fusion editing.

The matching editable backup, actual planning/Apply/history/key-edit recordings, complete live and finished playback, source clips/score/field artwork,59 decoded-frame contact sheet and17 preview/export pairs are included. All192 picture frames and complete audio decode. Exact document/compiler/worker/download hashes match. All333 protected files across five earlier delivery packages remain intact, including the rejected circle edit.

Faint strip seams and colour/edge differences remain in live preview; whole predictive picture/audio equality and real-time capture smoothness are not qualified. The separate exported movie has a clean reconstructed final shot. Recordings are silent QA captures; listen to the finished film. Human listening and owner creative approval remain open. Nothing was published, scheduled, deployed or purchased.
''')
